hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1070","We told Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, we told Malik, meaning Ibn Ismail, we told Yaqoub, h and Muhammad bin Othman Al-Ijli told us, we told Ubaid Allah I mean, Ibn Musa, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah Al-Qummi, on the authority of Issa bin Jariyah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed with us. May God bless him and grant him peace, in Ramadan, eight rak’ahs and the Witr prayer. When he was one of the midwives, we gathered in the mosque and hoped that he would come out to us, but he did not. He stayed in the mosque until the morning, then we went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we said to him: O Messenger of God, we hoped that you would come out. Come to us and lead us in prayer. He said: “I hate for Witr to be prescribed for you.”"
